From 3aebb3a38500aae1c2356c11e0fc21b13eb78b04 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mkinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 10:39:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(ui): start the GPU layer playback from the Simulate view

Slice S3c of the GPU stock sim (#2629). The transport starts the
playback worker in the layer mode when the window shell made a cutter
on the render device and the stock eye traces on the GPU. The cutter
runs the stock cut kernel on the render device (no second device), on
a hardware adapter only, and CAMCRAFT_GPU_COMPUTE=off turns it off. In
each other case the CPU playback of before starts. An eye that marches
a layer frame on the CPU ends the layer playback, and the CPU playback
starts in its place.

FieldPlay::set_layer keeps the layer mode off when no operation has an
f32 twin: a layer frame is always the whole layer, and the field's
patch frames are far smaller.

The playback cost bench gets a layer-mode walk. It shows that the two
reference programs of #3336 stay on the f64 field: each has an arc
move, and arcs have no twin until #2628.

Refs #3336
Refs #2629

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
